@page "/"
@layout MainLayout

<PageTitle>BevTools - in-app developer tools for Blazor</PageTitle>

@* The landing page: hero → proof strip → capability grid → code walkthrough → comparison with the
   browser's own dev tools → persona tiles → FAQ → final call to action. Everything else on the
   site is a documentation page under DocsLayout. The hero's live sample is BevTools itself: the
   panel is running on this page, and the button gives it one event to show. *@

<div class="bb-landing">

    @* ============================== Hero ============================== *@

    <section class="bb-hero">
        <div class="bb-hero-copy">
            <span class="bb-hero-eyebrow">
                <span class="bb-dot bb-dot-success"></span>
                Open source · MIT · net8.0 / net9.0 / net10.0
            </span>
            <h1>Dev tools for Blazor,<br /><span class="bb-hero-accent">inside your app.</span></h1>
            <p class="bb-hero-sub">
                A live component tree, a profiler that says <em>why</em> each component rendered, a timeline that links
                every click to what it caused, and inspectors for state, HTTP, JS interop, errors, DI and circuits -
                added with one line in <code>Program.cs</code> and no change to your components.
            </p>
            <pre class="bb-code bb-hero-install">dotnet add package Bit.BevTools</pre>
            <div class="bb-hero-actions">
                <a href="getting-started" class="btn btn-primary bb-btn-lg">Get started →</a>
                <a href="problems" class="btn btn-secondary bb-btn-lg">Problems to diagnose</a>
                <a class="btn btn-secondary bb-btn-lg" href="@SiteInfo.ProjectUrl" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub ↗</a>
            </div>
        </div>

        @* The setup, framed as a window, and underneath it the tool running on this very page. *@
        <div class="bb-hero-code">
            <div class="bb-browser">
                <div class="bb-browser-bar">
                    <span class="bb-browser-dots" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span>
                    <span class="bb-browser-url">Program.cs · MainLayout.razor</span>
                </div>
                <pre class="bb-code"><span class="c">// Program.cs</span>
builder.Services.AddBitBevToolsServerServices();

<span class="c">@@* MainLayout.razor *@@</span>
&lt;<span class="k">BevToolsPanel</span> /&gt;</pre>
                <div class="home-hero-live">
                    <p>
                        <strong>It is running here.</strong> Press <kbd>Ctrl</kbd><kbd>Shift</kbd><kbd>D</kbd> or the
                        ⚙ BevTools badge, open the <strong>Timeline</strong>, then click:
                    </p>
                    <div class="bb-toolbar">
                        <button type="button" class="btn btn-primary" id="hero-click" @onclick="Click">Clicked @_clicks @(_clicks == 1 ? "time" : "times")</button>
                        <span class="bb-muted">one <em>onclick → Home.Click</em> event, one render of <code>Home</code></span>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    @* ============================== Proof strip ============================== *@

    <section class="bb-proof">
        <div><strong>No source changes</strong><span>public hooks: the component activator, HTTP handlers, loggers</span></div>
        <div><strong>Never fakes data</strong><span>what it cannot observe, it says it cannot</span></div>
        <div><strong>Every render mode</strong><span>WebAssembly, Server, Auto and static SSR</span></div>
        <div><strong>Dormant in production</strong><span>on in Development only; off, it registers nothing</span></div>
    </section>

    @* ============================== Capability grid ============================== *@

    <section class="bb-section">
        <p class="bb-overline">Capabilities</p>
        <h2>The questions it answers</h2>
        <p class="bb-section-sub">
            Each panel answers a question that logs and breakpoints answer slowly. Every page of this site is a small
            app built to ask one of them - open the panel on it and look.
        </p>
        <div class="bb-grid">
            <section class="bb-card">
                <h3 class="bb-card-title"><span class="bb-dot bb-dot-primary"></span> Why did it render?</h3>
                <p class="bb-card-desc">
                    The component tree with parameters, cascading values, state and services - and for every render its
                    cause: an event, a parent re-render, a navigation or <code>StateHasChanged</code>.
                </p>
                <a href="dashboard" class="btn btn-outline">Dashboard →</a>
            </section>
            <section class="bb-card">
                <h3 class="bb-card-title"><span class="bb-dot bb-dot-warning"></span> What did this keystroke cost?</h3>
                <p class="bb-card-desc">
                    A profiler per instance and per type, render batches with their diff cost, and the rules that spot
                    render storms, cascades and renders forced by a parent.
                </p>
                <a href="products" class="btn btn-outline">Products →</a>
            </section>
            <section class="bb-card">
                <h3 class="bb-card-title"><span class="bb-dot bb-dot-success"></span> What happened when I clicked?</h3>
                <p class="bb-card-desc">
                    One timeline for renders, batches, events, navigation, state, HTTP, JS, errors and circuits, with
                    each entry linked to what caused it and to what it caused.
                </p>
                <a href="counter" class="btn btn-outline">Counter →</a>
            </section>
            <section class="bb-card">
                <h3 class="bb-card-title"><span class="bb-dot bb-dot-danger"></span> Which request failed?</h3>
                <p class="bb-card-desc">
                    Every <code>IHttpClientFactory</code> request with status, duration, headers (redacted) and the UI
                    event that sent it - including the ones a Blazor Server app makes on the server.
                </p>
                <a href="orders" class="btn btn-outline">Orders →</a>
            </section>
            <section class="bb-card">
                <h3 class="bb-card-title"><span class="bb-dot bb-dot-primary"></span> What changed in my state?</h3>
                <p class="bb-card-desc">
                    State containers that implement <code>IBevStateProvider</code> get a history of named actions with
                    before/after diffs and the click behind each one.
                </p>
                <a href="checkout" class="btn btn-outline">Checkout →</a>
            </section>
            <section class="bb-card">
                <h3 class="bb-card-title"><span class="bb-dot bb-dot-warning"></span> Which JS call is slow?</h3>
                <p class="bb-card-desc">
                    Interop calls per identifier with durations, failures and the component that made them, plus the
                    JS → .NET callbacks and the browser's storage, redacted.
                </p>
                <a href="interop" class="btn btn-outline">JS interop →</a>
            </section>
            <section class="bb-card">
                <h3 class="bb-card-title"><span class="bb-dot bb-dot-danger"></span> Where did that exception come from?</h3>
                <p class="bb-card-desc">
                    Errors from rendering, handlers, HTTP, interop and the browser, each with its component, its source
                    location and the ten timeline entries before it.
                </p>
                <a href="errors" class="btn btn-outline">Errors →</a>
            </section>
            <section class="bb-card">
                <h3 class="bb-card-title"><span class="bb-dot bb-dot-success"></span> Is my circuit blocked?</h3>
                <p class="bb-card-desc">
                    On Blazor Server: the circuit's lifecycle, connection state, time spent on each inbound message and
                    the reconnect attempts the browser reports.
                </p>
                <a href="circuit" class="btn btn-outline">Circuit →</a>
            </section>
            <section class="bb-card">
                <h3 class="bb-card-title"><span class="bb-dot bb-dot-primary"></span> Is my DI set up right?</h3>
                <p class="bb-card-desc">
                    Every registration with its lifetime and dependencies, and the mistakes that only fail later: a
                    singleton capturing a scoped service, a circular dependency.
                </p>
                <a href="problems#problem-8" class="btn btn-outline">Problem 8 →</a>
            </section>
        </div>
    </section>

    @* ============================== Code walkthrough ============================== *@

    <section class="bb-section">
        <p class="bb-overline">In practice</p>
        <h2>Three steps, and two of them are optional</h2>
        <div class="bb-walkthrough">
            <div class="bb-walkthrough-row">
                <div class="bb-walkthrough-copy">
                    <span class="bb-step">01</span>
                    <h3>Register it</h3>
                    <p>
                        One call in the server project, one in the <code>.Client</code> project of an Interactive Auto app.
                        It switches itself on in Development only.
                    </p>
                    <a href="getting-started">Getting started →</a>
                </div>
                <pre class="bb-code"><span class="c">// Server project</span>
builder.Services.AddBitBevToolsServerServices();

<span class="c">// .Client project</span>
builder.Services.AddBitBevToolsServices(o =&gt;
    o.Enabled = builder.HostEnvironment.IsDevelopment());</pre>
            </div>
            <div class="bb-walkthrough-row">
                <div class="bb-walkthrough-copy">
                    <span class="bb-step">02</span>
                    <h3>Expose your state</h3>
                    <p>
                        A state container that implements <code>IBevStateProvider</code> gets a history of named
                        changes with diffs. Register it once and the State panel shows it.
                    </p>
                    <a href="checkout">Checkout →</a>
                </div>
                <pre class="bb-code"><span class="k">public sealed class</span> CartState : IBevStateProvider
{
    <span class="k">public string</span> Name =&gt; <span class="s">"CartState"</span>;
    <span class="k">public event</span> Action&lt;BevStateChangeInfo&gt;? Changed;
    <span class="k">public object</span>? GetSnapshot() =&gt; <span class="k">this</span>;
    <span class="c">// … Changed?.Invoke(new BevStateChangeInfo("Add", product.Name));</span>
}

builder.Services.AddBevToolsStateProvider&lt;CartState&gt;();</pre>
            </div>
            <div class="bb-walkthrough-row">
                <div class="bb-walkthrough-copy">
                    <span class="bb-step">03</span>
                    <h3>Keep secrets out of it</h3>
                    <p>
                        Members, headers, query values and storage keys that look sensitive are redacted at capture time.
                        Mark the rest yourself, or hide a member or a component entirely.
                    </p>
                    <a href="problems#problem-7">Problem 7 →</a>
                </div>
                <pre class="bb-code"><span class="k">public sealed class</span> UserSession
{
    <span class="c">// Redacted by its name.</span>
    <span class="k">public string</span> AccessToken { <span class="k">get</span>; <span class="k">set</span>; } = <span class="s">"…"</span>;

    [BevToolsSensitive]
    <span class="k">public string</span> Nickname { <span class="k">get</span>; <span class="k">set</span>; } = <span class="s">"…"</span>;
}</pre>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    @* ============================== Comparison ============================== *@

    <section class="bb-section">
        <p class="bb-overline">Comparison</p>
        <h2>Why not the browser's dev tools?</h2>
        <p class="bb-section-sub">
            The browser sees the DOM, the requests the browser makes and JavaScript. A Blazor app's questions are about
            components, .NET state, the server and the renderer - and on Blazor Server most of it never reaches the
            browser at all.
        </p>
        <div class="bb-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="The browser's dev tools compared with BevTools">
            <table class="bb-table bb-compare">
                <thead>
                    <tr><th>Question</th><th>Browser dev tools</th><th>BevTools</th></tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr><td>Which components exist, with what parameters?</td><td>DOM elements only</td><td>The component tree, parameters, cascading values, state and services</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Why did this component render?</td><td>Not visible</td><td>A cause per render: event, parent, navigation, <code>StateHasChanged</code></td></tr>
                    <tr><td>HTTP calls of a Blazor Server app</td><td>Not visible - they are made by the server</td><td>Every <code>IHttpClientFactory</code> request with the UI event that sent it</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>JS interop on Blazor Server</td><td>SignalR frames</td><td>Calls per identifier, with duration, result and component</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>What is registered in DI?</td><td>Not visible</td><td>Lifetimes, dependencies, captive dependencies and cycles</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Is the circuit healthy?</td><td>A WebSocket</td><td>Lifecycle, connection state, inbound message time, reconnects</td></tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
    </section>

    @* ============================== Persona CTAs ============================== *@

    <section class="bb-section">
        <p class="bb-overline">Where to start</p>
        <h2>Choose your path</h2>
        <div class="bb-grid">
            <section class="bb-card">
                <h3 class="bb-card-title"><span class="bb-dot bb-dot-primary"></span> New to BevTools?</h3>
                <p class="bb-card-desc">Install, register, place the panel - and see your own app from the inside.</p>
                <a href="getting-started" class="btn btn-primary">Getting started →</a>
            </section>
            <section class="bb-card">
                <h3 class="bb-card-title"><span class="bb-dot bb-dot-success"></span> Want to practise first?</h3>
                <p class="bb-card-desc">Twenty real problems are planted in this app, each with the steps from the symptom to its cause.</p>
                <a href="problems" class="btn btn-outline">Problems to diagnose →</a>
            </section>
            <section class="bb-card">
                <h3 class="bb-card-title"><span class="bb-dot bb-dot-warning"></span> Writing a library?</h3>
                <p class="bb-card-desc">Contribute panels, state providers, diagnostic rules and commands through <code>IBevToolsExtension</code>.</p>
                <a href="@($"{SiteInfo.ProjectUrl}#extending")" class="btn btn-outline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Extending BevTools ↗</a>
            </section>
        </div>
    </section>

    @* ============================== FAQ ============================== *@

    <section class="bb-section">
        <p class="bb-overline">Questions</p>
        <h2>Frequently asked</h2>
        <div class="bb-faq">
            <details>
                <summary>Does it end up in production?</summary>
                <p>
                    Only if you ask it to. It is enabled when the host environment is <code>Development</code> unless
                    <code>options.Enabled</code> says otherwise, renders nothing during prerendering, and when disabled
                    registers no activator, handler or logger - a referenced but disabled BevTools measured at about 2 %
                    in the benchmark, inside its noise. This site turns it on explicitly so that you can try it.
                </p>
            </details>
            <details>
                <summary>Which .NET versions and render modes?</summary>
                <p>
                    .NET 8, 9 and 10, in WebAssembly, Server, Interactive Auto and static SSR. The render causes that
                    come from UI events and the framework's own timings need .NET 10; on .NET 8 and 9 those rows say
                    <em>Requires .NET 10</em> instead of showing nothing.
                </p>
            </details>
            <details>
                <summary>How does it see inside the app without changing it?</summary>
                <p>
                    Through public hooks - the component activator, an HTTP message handler filter, a logger provider, a
                    circuit handler - plus the framework's own activities and meters, and optional reflection over Blazor
                    internals that reports a capability as unavailable rather than failing when a member is missing.
                </p>
            </details>
            <details>
                <summary>What about passwords and tokens?</summary>
                <p>
                    Redacted when they are captured: by name (<code>password</code>, <code>token</code>,
                    <code>authorization</code>, …), by <code>[BevToolsSensitive]</code>, and in the browser before storage
                    values reach .NET. Request and response bodies are never read, nothing is sent anywhere, and an export
                    contains exactly what the panels show.
                </p>
            </details>
            <details>
                <summary>What does it cost?</summary>
                <p>
                    Roughly 0.4 µs and 0.4 KB per component render while recording, measured by a benchmark in the
                    repository, with every buffer bounded. The About panel reports what BevTools itself is costing the
                    running app.
                </p>
            </details>
            <details>
                <summary>Why does this site's header show up in the component tree?</summary>
                <p>
                    Because it is part of the app. The header, the docs layout and the footer of this site are ordinary
                    components, so BevTools lists them, profiles them and attributes their JS calls like any other - only
                    BevTools' own UI is left out.
                </p>
            </details>
        </div>
    </section>

    @* ============================== Final CTA ============================== *@

    <section class="bb-final-cta">
        <h2>Find the cause, not just the symptom</h2>
        <p class="bb-section-sub">One package, one line in Program.cs, one tag in your layout.</p>
        <pre class="bb-code bb-hero-install">dotnet add package Bit.BevTools</pre>
        <div class="bb-hero-actions">
            <a href="getting-started" class="btn btn-primary bb-btn-lg">Get started →</a>
            <a href="problems" class="btn btn-secondary bb-btn-lg">Problems to diagnose</a>
        </div>
    </section>
</div>

@code {
    private int _clicks;

    // A named method rather than a lambda, so the Timeline's entry for the click reads "Home.Click".
    private void Click() => _clicks++;
}
